{"id": "EUVD-2026-103692", "enisaUuid": "9de1d800-7be1-33d0-b7c8-32c35fef7179", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb: client: clean up failed cached directory opens\n\nopen_cached_dir() sends CREATE and QUERY_INFO as a compound request. If\nthe CREATE succeeds but a later command returns an error, the function\nmust retain the CREATE FID so common cleanup can issue SMB2_close(). It\nalso must not treat a response error as a valid CREATE.\n\nValidate the CREATE response before using its fields, record the FIDs, and\nmark the handle open before handling errors from later compound commands.\nMove the -EREMCHG reconnect handling before response validation so a\nmissing response does not hide the reconnect request. Count the handle\nwhen it is marked open; confirmed close responses decrement the counter,\nwhile existing close retry behavior remains best effort on transport\nfailures.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:15:02", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:19:47", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/48958ddda3d7eee3600261e2d90671f63e055dc4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/abab661eed00fa102d3c35ddf1cce4f687e718c1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/7c1509598a4fdfb54cb09ce33e4405bd6dbd8295", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d2ff5fb93ea83034025850266b5eed391f96b825"], "aliases": ["GHSA-h9j7-fw85-wm4j", "CVE-2026-98452"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "02a93ac6-7c70-37e3-bed8-6f9d8fb40655", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "10ab1df7-3b3d-3b43-af8b-470dc414cc31", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.112"}, {"id": "17e69096-01b0-343d-9d5d-e673688ef85f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.55"}, {"id": "2af4d692-e2dd-3951-97da-2df4864405e7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.1"}, {"id": "5e065de9-183a-3e8f-a2b7-09e3a7d102db", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b0f6df737a1c5d9d5ff90cc946205d8af46cc067 <7c1509598a4fdfb54cb09ce33e4405bd6dbd8295"}, {"id": "5ecf578a-61bb-33fa-bac3-280fdd61fea6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "62eccbb6-9a84-3c28-9cb5-e019b044f46c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b0f6df737a1c5d9d5ff90cc946205d8af46cc067 <abab661eed00fa102d3c35ddf1cce4f687e718c1"}, {"id": "768cab7d-ecc6-3838-a307-d03c20b0e8b3", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b0f6df737a1c5d9d5ff90cc946205d8af46cc067 <48958ddda3d7eee3600261e2d90671f63e055dc4"}, {"id": "a0dce600-b4c9-313a-93c5-2441961993a4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "b0f6df737a1c5d9d5ff90cc946205d8af46cc067 <d2ff5fb93ea83034025850266b5eed391f96b825"}, {"id": "e5f249f5-d099-39e6-a6a8-0d749789fd36", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "eedcb385-aaeb-3c06-9ffd-e3ab61cb9660", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}